gottailcall_* -- the fixtures for option gottailcall (GH-904): tail calls
through a GOT slot, each caller placed before its callee
(tests/cli/gottailcall-*.json).

What they are
  gottailcall_x86_64.so  x86-64 shared object built -fno-plt -Wl,-z,now:
                         g, fwd3 and tick end in jmp *f@GOTPCREL(%rip); h
                         jumps through the undefined ext's slot.
  gottailcall_mipsel.o   little-endian MIPS32 PIC relocatable object: g,
                         fwd3, tick and h end in lw $t9,%call16(f)($gp);
                         jr $t9, and h's slot names the undefined ext.
  Source: gottailcall.c.

Why they are vendored
  The MIPS object needs a cross gcc CI does not have, and the order of
  functions in both (callers first) decides which arm of the option runs.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu gcc 11.4.0 and mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc 10.3.0:

      gcc -O2 -fno-toplevel-reorder -fPIC -fno-plt -shared -Wl,-z,now \
          -Wl,--build-id=none -o gottailcall_x86_64.so gottailcall.c
      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -fno-toplevel-reorder -fPIC -c gottailcall.c \
          -o gottailcall_mipsel.o

  sha256:
    a0a97b04204117a92a35b818e548f394595082b64d8ee7126ea3f893f1c6b1f6  gottailcall_x86_64.so
    6769679c5eabedc1b5fa8c757c2d70528624a8bc51e6bf3fab89e08eb4aef10c  gottailcall_mipsel.o
